  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project skill and locating the storefront cart API so the quantity limit can follow the existing cart flow.The cart writes go through one facade. I'll read the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` on each request and reject a line above that limit before anything is saved.A cart line on the storefront cart API can now hold at most N units. N comes from the store merchant configuration key `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY`, read on each request so a change applies without a restart, and defaults to 99 when the store has no value. Creating a cart, adding a line, or changing a quantity above N (`POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`, including an add that would push an existing line over N) is rejected with HTTP 400 before the cart is saved. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=CartLineQuantityPolicyTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 and an unchanged cart on the live storefront cart endpoints\"], \"missing\": [\"a running Shopizer instance and the ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest fixture\"]}",
